@@ -72,6 +72,26 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Waiting for an event
+
+`EventEmitter.waitFor(event, options?)` returns a Promise that resolves with a
+new array containing the arguments from the next occurrence of the event. The
+event listener is registered synchronously, so an emit immediately after the
+call is observed. Each waiter is independent and supports string or symbol
+events, including events with no arguments or more than five arguments.
+
+Pass an `AbortSignal` as `options.signal` to cancel a pending wait. A
+pre-aborted signal rejects immediately, and aborting a pending wait rejects it
+with the signal's exact reason. The first event or abort settles the Promise;
+later events and aborts have no effect. Ordinary `off`, `removeListener`, or
+`removeAllListeners` calls remove the listener but do not settle the Promise.
+If a signal was supplied, aborting after ordinary removal still rejects the
+Promise and cleans up its abort handler.
+
+```js
+var result = await EE.waitFor('data', { signal: controller.signal });
+```
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
